\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 **Layer A Prompt \'97 Impression Capture (Baseline)**\
\
*Governing frame: /adopted/session-opening-protocol.md*\
\
You are developing Layer A of the SageReasoning Agent Trust Layer wrapper \'97 the impression capture baseline. This layer intercepts agent input before response generation and produces a structured examination record. Your task:\
\
(1) Define the minimum viable impression record: what fields must be captured (input classification, genuine good/evil/indifferent, passion pattern if detectable, confidence score) and what format serves both the trust layer and developer debugging.\
\
(2) Design the examination as a timed operation. The layer must record how long the examination took, because examination depth and speed are both trust-relevant signals. Fast shallow examinations and slower thorough ones are not equivalent \'97 the scoring must reflect this.\
\
(3) Define what "examination happened" means operationally \'97 what artifact proves the pause occurred and can be audited independently of the agent's response.\
\
(4) Specify the baseline trust metric: impression capture rate (percentage of inputs examined before response) and examination time distribution.\
\
Constraint: Design for an agent of unknown internal structure. The wrapper cannot assume access to the agent's reasoning process \'97 it can only intercept input and output. Keep the examination as lightweight as possible while preserving genuine signal. Output: structured specification for Layer A with field definitions, timing requirements, and baseline trust metric formula.\
